/* ---------------- 17: There is / are; some, any, no ---------------- */
VOC(17, {
  vi: 'some / any / no / every so‘zlari va ulardan yasalgan «kimdir, hech narsa, hamma joy» kabi so‘zlar.',
  vr: [{ h: 'some-, any-, no-, every-', x: '<p><b>some-</b> — darak gapda: There’s <b>somebody</b> at the door.</p><p><b>any-</b> — so‘roq va inkor gapda: Is there <b>anything</b> in the fridge? I don’t know <b>anybody</b> here.</p><p><b>no-</b> — fe’l <b>darak</b> shaklda bo‘lganda: There’s <b>nothing</b> in the box. (Ikki inkor yo‘q: «There isn’t nothing» — xato!)</p><p><b>every-</b> — hamma: <b>everybody</b>, <b>everything</b>. Ular birlikda: Everybody <b>is</b> here.</p>',
    tb: { h: ['', 'kishi', 'narsa', 'joy'], r: [['some-', 'somebody', 'something', 'somewhere'], ['any-', 'anybody', 'anything', 'anywhere'], ['no-', 'nobody', 'nothing', 'nowhere'], ['every-', 'everybody', 'everything', 'everywhere']] } }],
  V: [
    { g: 'base', t: 'Asosiy so‘zlar', w: [
      ['there is', '/ðeər ˈɪz/', '… bor (birlik)', '*There is* a bank near my house.', 'Uyim yonida bank bor.', 'bank'],
      ['there are', '/ðeər ˈɑː/', '… bor (ko‘plik)', '*There are* thirty pupils in my class.', 'Sinfimda o‘ttizta o‘quvchi bor.', 'busts-in-silhouette'],
      ['some', '/sʌm/', 'bir oz, bir nechta', 'There are *some* apples on the table.', 'Stolda bir nechta olma bor.', 'red-apple'],
      ['any', '/ˈeni/', 'hech qanday; biror (so‘roq)', 'Are there *any* questions?', 'Savollar bormi?', '?'],
      ['no', '/nəʊ/', 'hech qanday … yo‘q', 'There’s *no* milk in the fridge.', 'Muzlatgichda sut yo‘q.', 'glass-of-milk !'],
      ['else', '/els/', 'boshqa, yana', 'Do you want anything *else*?', 'Yana biror narsa xohlaysizmi?', 'plus']
    ] },
    { g: 'body', t: 'Kishi: -body', w: [
      ['somebody', '/ˈsʌmbədi/', 'kimdir', '*Somebody* is knocking at the door.', 'Kimdir eshikni taqillatyapti.', 'door bust-in-silhouette'],
      ['anybody', '/ˈenibɒdi/', 'biror kishi; hech kim (inkor)', 'Is *anybody* at home?', 'Uyda biror kishi bormi?', 'house ?'],
      ['nobody', '/ˈnəʊbədi/', 'hech kim', '*Nobody* knows the answer.', 'Javobni hech kim bilmaydi.', 'bust-in-silhouette !'],
      ['everybody', '/ˈevribɒdi/', 'hamma, har kim', '*Everybody* loves plov.', 'Hamma palovni yaxshi ko‘radi.', 'busts-in-silhouette red-heart']
    ] },
    { g: 'thing', t: 'Narsa: -thing', w: [
      ['something', '/ˈsʌmθɪŋ/', 'nimadir', 'I have *something* for you.', 'Senga bir narsam bor.', 'wrapped-gift'],
      ['anything', '/ˈeniθɪŋ/', 'biror narsa; hech narsa (inkor)', 'I can’t see *anything*. It’s dark.', 'Hech narsani ko‘rmayapman. Qorong‘i.', 'eyes ?'],
      ['nothing', '/ˈnʌθɪŋ/', 'hech narsa', 'There’s *nothing* in my pocket.', 'Cho‘ntagimda hech narsa yo‘q.', 'empty-nest'],
      ['everything', '/ˈevriθɪŋ/', 'hamma narsa', '*Everything* is ready.', 'Hamma narsa tayyor.', 'check-mark-button']
    ] },
    { g: 'where', t: 'Joy: -where', w: [
      ['somewhere', '/ˈsʌmweə/', 'qayergadir, qayerdadir', 'My keys are *somewhere* in this room.', 'Kalitlarim shu xonada qayerdadir.', 'key magnifying-glass-tilted-left'],
      ['anywhere', '/ˈeniweə/', 'biror joyda; hech qayerda (inkor)', 'I can’t find my phone *anywhere*.', 'Telefonimni hech qayerdan topa olmayapman.', 'mobile-phone ?'],
      ['nowhere', '/ˈnəʊweə/', 'hech qayerda, hech qayerga', 'There’s *nowhere* to sit.', 'O‘tirishga hech qayer yo‘q.', 'chair !'],
      ['everywhere', '/ˈevriweə/', 'hamma joyda', 'There are flowers *everywhere*.', 'Hamma joyda gullar bor.', 'tulip+blossom+sunflower']
    ] }
  ],
  A: [{
    k: 'Sirli hikoya', t: 'The Night Visitor at School 25', s: 'Kechasi maktabda kim bor edi? Qorovul Hamid aka bu sirni ochadi',
    p: [
      ['Hamid aka is the night guard at School 25. Every night, he walks [everywhere] in the building. [Everything] is usually quiet. [Nobody] is there after ten o’clock — just Hamid aka and his cup of tea.',
       'Hamid aka 25-maktabning tungi qorovuli. Har kecha u binoning hamma joyini aylanib chiqadi. Odatda hamma narsa tinch bo‘ladi. Soat o‘ndan keyin u yerda hech kim bo‘lmaydi — faqat Hamid aka va uning bir piyola choyi.'],
      ['But last Tuesday, at midnight, he heard [something] on the second floor. “Is [anybody] there?” he shouted. [There was|there is] no answer. He went up the stairs. [There were|there are] [some] books on the floor of the library, but he couldn’t see [anything] [else].',
       'Lekin o‘tgan seshanba, yarim tunda, u ikkinchi qavatda nimadir eshitdi. «Kim bor?» deb baqirdi. Javob bo‘lmadi. U zinadan ko‘tarildi. Kutubxona polida bir nechta kitob yotardi, lekin boshqa hech narsani ko‘ra olmadi.'],
      ['The next night, the same thing happened. This time, [there was|there is] a sandwich in the teachers’ room — but [there was|there is] [no] bread in the school kitchen! “[Somebody] is in the school,” he thought. “Maybe a student is hiding [somewhere].” There weren’t [any] cameras in the school. He looked in every classroom, but [there wasn’t|there is] [anybody] [anywhere].',
       'Keyingi kecha ham xuddi shunday bo‘ldi. Bu safar o‘qituvchilar xonasida sendvich bor edi — lekin maktab oshxonasida non yo‘q edi! «Maktabda kimdir bor, — deb o‘yladi u. — Balki biror o‘quvchi qayerdadir yashiringandir.» Maktabda hech qanday kamera yo‘q edi. U har bir sinfga qaradi, lekin hech qayerda hech kim yo‘q edi.'],
      ['On Thursday, Hamid aka put a camera in the library. In the morning, [everybody] came to watch the video: the head teacher, the cleaners and the Year 11 students. At 12:15 a.m., the library door opened… and [nothing] came in. Then a small grey face appeared — a cat!',
       'Payshanba kuni Hamid aka kutubxonaga kamera o‘rnatdi. Ertalab videoni ko‘rish uchun hamma keldi: direktor, farroshlar va 11-sinf o‘quvchilari. Tungi 12:15 da kutubxona eshigi ochildi… va hech narsa kirmadi. Keyin kichkina kulrang yuz paydo bo‘ldi — mushuk ekan!'],
      ['The cat lived in the school basement. It had [nowhere] else to go in the cold weather. It took the sandwich from the teachers’ room, and it jumped on the shelves and pushed the books. Now the cat has a name — Kitobxon — and a warm bed in the library. And [nobody] is scared of the night visitor any more.',
       'Mushuk maktab yerto‘lasida yashar ekan. Sovuq havoda boradigan boshqa hech qayeri yo‘q edi. U o‘qituvchilar xonasidan sendvichni olgan, tokchalarga sakrab kitoblarni itarib tushirgan. Endi mushukning ismi bor — Kitobxon — va kutubxonada iliq joyi bor. Endi hech kim tungi mehmondan qo‘rqmaydi.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What is Hamid aka’s job?', ['teacher', 'night guard', 'cleaner'], 1],
      ['What did he find on the library floor?', ['some books', 'a sandwich', 'a cat'], 0],
      ['Why was the sandwich strange?', ['It was very big.', 'There was no bread in the school kitchen.', 'It was in the library.'], 1],
      ['Where did Hamid aka put a camera?', ['in the kitchen', 'in the library', 'in the basement'], 1],
      ['Who was the night visitor?', ['a Year 11 student', 'a cleaner', 'a cat'], 2]
    ]
  }]
});

/* ---------------- 18: Food, quantities ---------------- */
