/* ---------------- 28: Modal Verbs ---------------- */
VOC(28, {
  vi: 'Modal fe’llar va ularga yaqin iboralar: imkoniyat, ruxsat, majburiyat, taqiq, maslahat va muloyim so‘rov.',
  vr: [{ h: 'must, have to, mustn’t, don’t have to', x: '<p><b>must</b> — gapiruvchining o‘zi zarur deb hisoblaydi: I <b>must</b> study harder.</p><p><b>have to</b> — qoida yoki tashqi majburiyat: We <b>have to</b> wear a uniform.</p><p><b>mustn’t</b> — taqiq (mumkin emas!): You <b>mustn’t</b> use phones in exams.</p><p><b>don’t have to / needn’t</b> — shart emas (lekin mumkin): You <b>don’t have to</b> come.</p><p>Modal fe’ldan keyin fe’l <b>to</b>siz va <b>-s</b>siz: She <b>can swim</b> («can to swim», «cans» — xato).</p>',
    tb: { h: ['Ma’no', 'Modal'], r: [['Qobiliyat', 'can, could, be able to'], ['Ehtimol', 'may, might, could'], ['Majburiyat', 'must, have to'], ['Taqiq', 'mustn’t, can’t'], ['Shart emas', 'don’t have to, needn’t'], ['Maslahat', 'should, shouldn’t'], ['Taklif', 'Shall we…?, Would you like…?']] } }],
  V: [
    { g: 'ability', t: 'Qobiliyat va ehtimol', w: [
      ['could', '/kʊd/', 'qila olardi (o‘tgan zamon); mumkin', 'I *could* read when I was four.', 'To‘rt yoshimda o‘qiy olardim.', 'open-book child'],
      ['be able to', '/bi ˈeɪbl tə/', 'qila olmoq', 'One day I’ll *be able to* speak five languages.', 'Bir kun kelib beshta tilda gapira olaman.', 'speaking-head'],
      ['may', '/meɪ/', 'balki; mumkin (ruxsat)', 'It *may* rain this afternoon.', 'Tushdan keyin yomg‘ir yog‘ishi mumkin.', 'sun-behind-rain-cloud'],
      ['might', '/maɪt/', 'balki (kamroq ehtimol)', 'I *might* go to the party, but I’m not sure.', 'Balki ziyofatga borarman, lekin aniq emas.', 'thinking-face']
    ] },
    { g: 'must', t: 'Majburiyat va taqiq', w: [
      ['must', '/mʌst/', 'shart, kerak (majburiyat)', 'I *must* finish this today.', 'Buni bugun tugatishim shart.', 'warning'],
      ['have to', '/ˈhæv tə/', 'majbur bo‘lmoq (qoida)', 'We *have to* wear a uniform at school.', 'Maktabda forma kiyishimiz shart.', 'necktie'],
      ['mustn’t', '/ˈmʌsnt/', 'mumkin emas (taqiq)', 'You *mustn’t* use your phone in the exam.', 'Imtihonda telefondan foydalanish mumkin emas.', 'mobile-phone-off'],
      ['don’t have to', '/ˌdəʊnt ˈhæv tə/', 'shart emas', 'You *don’t have to* come, but you can.', 'Kelishingiz shart emas, lekin kelsangiz bo‘ladi.', 'person-shrugging'],
      ['needn’t', '/ˈniːdnt/', 'kerak emas, hojati yo‘q', 'You *needn’t* bring food. We have a lot.', 'Ovqat olib kelishingizning hojati yo‘q. Ko‘p.', 'fork-and-knife-with-plate check-mark-button']
    ] },
    { g: 'advice', t: 'Maslahat, taklif va so‘rov', w: [
      ['should', '/ʃʊd/', '…ish kerak (maslahat)', 'You *should* see a doctor.', 'Shifokorga ko‘rinishingiz kerak.', 'stethoscope'],
      ['shouldn’t', '/ˈʃʊdnt/', '…ish kerak emas (maslahat)', 'You *shouldn’t* eat so many sweets.', 'Bunchalik ko‘p shirinlik yemasligingiz kerak.', 'candy'],
      ['Shall we…?', '/ʃæl wiː/', '…aylikmi?', '*Shall we* go to the cinema?', 'Kinoga boraylikmi?', 'popcorn ?'],
      ['Would you like…?', '/wʊd juː ˈlaɪk/', '…ni xohlaysizmi?', '*Would you like* some tea?', 'Choy ichasizmi?', 'teacup-without-handle ?'],
      ['Could you…?', '/kʊd juː/', '… olasizmi? (muloyim so‘rov)', '*Could you* open the window, please?', 'Derazani ochib bera olasizmi, iltimos?', 'window ?']
    ] }
  ],
  A: [{
    k: 'Dunyo bo‘ylab', t: 'School Rules Around the World', s: 'Turli mamlakatlarda o‘quvchilar nima qilishi shart va nima qilishi mumkin emas?',
    p: [
      ['Every school has rules. But the rules are very different around the world. Here are some interesting examples. Which school would you like to go to?',
       'Har bir maktabning qoidalari bor. Lekin qoidalar dunyo bo‘ylab juda farq qiladi. Mana ba’zi qiziq misollar. Qaysi maktabda o‘qishni xohlardingiz?'],
      ['In Japan, students [have to] clean their classrooms every day — there are no cleaners! They [mustn’t] wear shoes inside; they [have to] change into special slippers. Students [could|could] get into trouble if their hair colour isn’t natural.',
       'Yaponiyada o‘quvchilar har kuni sinflarini tozalashlari shart — farroshlar yo‘q! Ular ichkarida poyabzal kiyishi mumkin emas, maxsus shippakka almashtirishlari kerak. Agar sochining rangi tabiiy bo‘lmasa, o‘quvchi muammoga duch kelishi mumkin.'],
      ['In Finland, children [don’t have to] wear a uniform, and they [needn’t] do much homework. They start school at seven, but by 15 most of them are [able to|be able to] speak three languages. Teachers say children [should] play outside every day, even in winter.',
       'Finlyandiyada bolalar forma kiyishi shart emas, ko‘p uy vazifasi qilishining ham hojati yo‘q. Ular maktabga yetti yoshda boradi, lekin 15 yoshga borib ko‘pchiligi uchta tilda gapira oladi. Ustozlarning aytishicha, bolalar har kuni, hatto qishda ham tashqarida o‘ynashi kerak.'],
      ['In Uzbekistan, students [must] stand up when the teacher comes in. You [shouldn’t] talk during the lesson, and in many schools you [mustn’t] use your phone at all. But break time is fun. A friend [may] ask you, “[Shall we…?|Shall we…?] play football?” or “[Would you like…?|Would you like…?] some of my somsa?”',
       'O‘zbekistonda ustoz kirganda o‘quvchilar o‘rnidan turishi shart. Dars paytida gaplashmaslik kerak, ko‘p maktablarda esa telefondan umuman foydalanish mumkin emas. Lekin tanaffus qiziqarli. Do‘stingiz: «Futbol o‘ynaylikmi?» yoki «Somsamdan yeysanmi?» deb so‘rashi mumkin.'],
      ['What about the future? Some experts say that schools [might] not have classrooms in 2050. Students [could] study at home with AI teachers. But one rule will never change: if you need help, you can always say, “[Could you…?|Could you…?] help me, please?”',
       'Kelajak-chi? Ba’zi mutaxassislarning aytishicha, 2050-yilda maktablarda sinfxonalar bo‘lmasligi mumkin. O‘quvchilar uyda sun’iy intellekt ustozlar bilan o‘qishi mumkin. Lekin bitta qoida hech qachon o‘zgarmaydi: yordam kerak bo‘lsa, doim «Menga yordam bera olasizmi, iltimos?» deyishingiz mumkin.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What do students in Japan have to do every day?', ['wear a uniform', 'clean their classrooms', 'play outside'], 1],
      ['What don’t children in Finland have to do?', ['wear a uniform', 'go to school', 'speak English'], 0],
      ['At what age do Finnish children start school?', ['five', 'six', 'seven'], 2],
      ['What must students in Uzbekistan do when the teacher comes in?', ['stand up', 'sit down', 'say goodbye'], 0],
      ['What might schools not have in 2050?', ['teachers', 'classrooms', 'rules'], 1]
    ]
  }]
});

