  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Girl Who Took Up Pottery at Seventeen', s: 'Rishtonda bo‘sh vaqtda boshlangan hobbi qanday kasbga aylanadi',
    p: [
      ['Munisa had never been a creative person. In her [spare time|spare time] she used to scroll through her phone. “I need [a way to relax|a way to relax],” she told her grandmother. Her grandmother, a [passionate] [hobbyist], answered, “[Take up|take up] something with your hands. Cooking, [knitting], [gardening], [baking]… try anything.” Munisa laughed. “They’re not [my cup of tea|it’s not my cup of tea]. Maybe [stargazing] or [birdwatching]?” She tried both, but nothing felt right.',
       'Munisa hech qachon ijodkor odam bo‘lmagan. Bo‘sh vaqtida telefonini varaqlab o‘tirardi. «Menga dam olish usuli kerak», dedi u buvisiga. Buvisi — ishtiyoqli havaskor — shunday javob berdi: «Qo‘ling bilan biror ish boshla. Ovqat pishirish, to‘qish, bog‘dorchilik, pishiriq… istalganini sinab ko‘r.» Munisa kuldi. «Bular menga to‘g‘ri kelmaydi. Balki yulduzlarni yoki qushlarni kuzatarman?» U ikkalasini ham sinab ko‘rdi, lekin hech narsa yoqmadi.'],
      ['One Saturday the family went [hiking|hiking] near Rishtan, and they visited a workshop where an old master was making [pottery|pottery]. Munisa watched his hands for an hour and [lost track of time|lose track of time]. The master said, “You are a [beginner], but you have the eye. Come on Monday.” Munisa [joined a club|join a club] at the workshop, and she began to [take up|take up] ceramics seriously. [Practice makes perfect|practice makes perfect], the master repeated.',
       'Bir shanba kuni oila Rishton yaqinida tog‘ yurishiga chiqdi va keksa usta kulolchilik qilayotgan ustaxonaga kirishdi. Munisa bir soat ustaning qo‘llariga qaradi va vaqtni unutdi. Usta: «Sen boshlovchisan, lekin ko‘zing o‘tkir. Dushanba kel», dedi. Munisa ustaxonadagi klubga qo‘shildi va keramika bilan jiddiy shug‘ullana boshladi. «Mashq mukammallik beradi», deb takrorlardi usta.'],
      ['At first it was a [challenge]. Her bowls were crooked, and the clay kept breaking. It was [time-consuming] and tiring. She wanted to [quit], but the master said, “You’ll [get the hang of|get the hang of] it.” She worked [regularly], three evenings a week, and [occasionally] on Sundays. She [got better at|get better at] it slowly. Soon the skill became [addictive] — she thought about clay all day. She became [keen on|be keen on] glazing and [crazy about|be crazy about] ancient patterns.',
       'Avvaliga bu sinov edi. Uning kosalari qiyshiq chiqdi, loy esa tez-tez sinardi. Bu ko‘p vaqt oladigan va charchatadigan edi. U voz kechmoqchi bo‘ldi, lekin usta: «Uddasidan chiqa boshlaysan», dedi. U muntazam, haftada uch kech ishladi, ba’zan yakshanba ham. Asta-sekin yaxshilandi. Tez orada bu ko‘nikma odatga aylandi — kun bo‘yi loy haqida o‘ylar edi. U sirlashga qiziqib qoldi va qadimiy naqshlarning ishqibozi bo‘ldi.'],
      ['Months later her first big [achievement] came: a local museum bought her vase for its [collection]. A newspaper called her an [inspiring] young [enthusiast]. Munisa modestly said it was just a [pastime|pastime]. But everyone could see she was [seriously|seriously] good. “It’s so [rewarding|rewarding],” she said. “I’ve found a real [skill] that makes me happy.” Her grandmother was proud: “I knew it was a good idea!”',
       'Oylar o‘tgach birinchi katta yutug‘i keldi: mahalliy muzey uning vazasini to‘plami uchun sotib oldi. Gazeta uni ilhomlantiruvchi yosh ishqibozi deb atadi. Munisa kamtarlik bilan bu shunchaki mashg‘ulot ekanini aytdi. Lekin hamma uning jiddiy yaxshi ekanini ko‘rib turardi. «Bu juda mamnuniyat beradi, — dedi u. — Meni xursand qiladigan haqiqiy ko‘nikma topdim.» Buvisi faxrlandi: «Men bu yaxshi g‘oya ekanini bilgan edim!»'],
      ['Today Munisa teaches [calligraphy] and pottery on weekends, and [stargazing] is just a [way to relax|a way to relax] now. To [stay in shape|stay in shape], she walks to the workshop every morning. Her advice? “Don’t think you must be talented. Just start. The first bowl is always a [piece of cake|a piece of cake] compared with the second!” she laughs.',
       'Bugun Munisa dam olish kunlari xattotlik va kulolchilikdan dars beradi, yulduzlarni kuzatish esa endi shunchaki dam olish usuli. Sog‘lom bo‘lish uchun har ertalab ustaxonaga piyoda boradi. Uning maslahati? «Iste’dodli bo‘lishim kerak deb o‘ylamang. Shunchaki boshlang. Birinchi kosa har doim ikkinchisiga nisbatan juda oson!» deb kuladi u.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['Why did Munisa’s grandmother tell her to take up a hobby?', ['She needed a way to relax.', 'She was ill.', 'She had no friends.'], 0],
      ['Where did Munisa discover pottery?', ['in Rishtan', 'in Khiva', 'at school'], 0],
      ['What was difficult at first?', ['Her bowls were crooked and the clay kept breaking.', 'There was no club.', 'She had no time.'], 0],
      ['What was her first big achievement?', ['A museum bought her vase.', 'She won a race.', 'She opened a shop.'], 0],
      ['What is her advice?', ['Just start.', 'Wait for talent.', 'Give up quickly.'], 0]
    ]
  }],
