  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Headline That Went Viral', s: 'Bitta sarlavha qanday qilib butun shaharni bezovta qildi',
    p: [
      ['One Monday morning the [headline] on the [front page] of a local paper read: “MAYOR RESIGNS!” The paper was a [tabloid] with a large [circulation], and many people had a [subscription]. The [reporter] who wrote it was young and eager, and his [editor] liked [sensational] stories. By noon the news was [breaking|breaking] on the radio, and the TV [anchor] repeated it with great [coverage]. Soon the story was on every [column] in the city.',
       'Bir dushanba kuni ertalab mahalliy gazetaning birinchi sahifasidagi sarlavha shunday edi: «MERI ISTEFO BERDI!» Gazeta katta tirajli tabloid edi va ko‘pchilik unga obuna bo‘lgan edi. Uni yozgan muxbir yosh va g‘ayratli edi, muharriri esa shov-shuvli hikoyalarni yaxshi ko‘rardi. Tushga kelib yangilik radioda shoshilinch yangilik sifatida berildi va teleboshlovchi uni keng yoritish bilan takrorladi. Tez orada hikoya shahardagi har bir ustunda paydo bo‘ldi.'],
      ['But was it true? A [columnist] named Aziza was suspicious. “A [credible] story needs a real [source],” she said. “This one looks [biased], and I think the paper wanted to [mislead] people.” She decided to [verify|verify] it and [fact-check] every sentence. A [correspondent] from the town hall told her, [off the record|off the record], that the mayor had only gone on holiday. The press office had even issued a [press release] earlier, but nobody read it.',
       'Lekin bu rost edimi? Aziza ismli ustun muallifi shubhalandi. «Ishonchli hikoyaga haqiqiy manba kerak, — dedi u. — Bu tarafkash ko‘rinadi va menimcha, gazeta odamlarni chalg‘itmoqchi bo‘lgan.» U buni tasdiqlashga va har bir gapni tekshirishga qaror qildi. Shahar hokimiyatidagi maxsus muxbir unga rasmiy bo‘lmagan holda meri faqat ta’tilga chiqqanini aytdi. Matbuot xizmati hatto oldinroq matbuot xabarini tarqatgan edi, lekin buni hech kim o‘qimadi.'],
      ['Meanwhile a famous [influencer] shared the headline, and it [went viral|go viral]. Rumours began to [spread] faster than the truth. Some people said the government wanted to [censor] the real reason. Even the [paparazzi] gathered in front of the mayor’s house, and an [audience] of thousands followed the story online. A [documentary] crew asked for an interview. “Is it really [newsworthy]?” Aziza asked. “[Allegedly], he left. [Reportedly], he’s sick. Nobody knows.”',
       'Shu orada mashhur influenser sarlavhani ulashdi va u tez ommalashdi. Mish-mishlar haqiqatdan tezroq tarqala boshladi. Ba’zilar hukumat haqiqiy sababni senzuradan o‘tkazmoqchi, dedi. Paparatsilar hatto meri uyi oldiga to‘plandi va minglab auditoriya hikoyani onlayn kuzatdi. Hujjatli film guruhi intervyu so‘radi. «Bu haqiqatan ham yangilik bo‘larlimi?» deb so‘radi Aziza. «Da’vo qilinishicha, u ketgan. Xabar qilinishicha, u kasal. Hech kim bilmaydi.»'],
      ['In the end Aziza’s [objective] article was [published|publish] on Wednesday. It [made headlines|make headlines] too: “MAYOR ON HOLIDAY, NOT RESIGNING.” The TV channel had to [broadcast] a correction. “You have to [read between the lines|read between the lines],” Aziza told her readers. “Do not trust [word of mouth|word of mouth]. The newest news, [hot off the press|hot off the press], is not always the truest.” The mayor came back with a tan, and the editor of the tabloid quietly resigned.',
       'Oxir-oqibat Azizaning xolis maqolasi chorshanba kuni chop etildi. U ham sarlavhalarga chiqdi: «MERI TA’TILDA, ISTEFOGA CHIQMAGAN.» Telekanal tuzatishni efirga uzatishga majbur bo‘ldi. «Satr orasini o‘qish kerak, — dedi Aziza o‘quvchilariga. — Og‘izdan-og‘izga gaplarga ishonmang. Eng yangi, hozirgina chop etilgan yangilik doim ham eng to‘g‘risi emas.» Meri ko‘kargan teri bilan qaytdi, tabloid muharriri esa jimgina iste’foga chiqdi.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What was the headline?', ['MAYOR RESIGNS!', 'MAYOR ILL', 'MAYOR LOST'], 0],
      ['What kind of newspaper was it?', ['A tabloid', 'A magazine', 'A school paper'], 0],
      ['What did the correspondent tell Aziza?', ['The mayor was on holiday.', 'The mayor was arrested.', 'The mayor was ill.'], 0],
      ['What helped the story spread?', ['An influencer shared it.', 'A TV film', 'A letter'], 0],
      ['What did Aziza write?', ['An objective article', 'A biased column', 'A press release'], 0]
    ]
  }],
  vt: {
    wf: [
      ['inform', [['information', 'ma’lumot'], ['informative', 'ma’lumotli'], ['misinformation', 'noto‘g‘ri ma’lumot']], 'This is *misinformation*.'],
      ['publish', [['publication', 'nashr'], ['publisher', 'nashriyotchi'], ['published', 'chop etilgan']], 'The *publisher* is famous.'],
      ['journal', [['journalism', 'jurnalistika'], ['journalistic', 'jurnalistik'], ['journalist', 'jurnalist']], 'She studies *journalism*.'],
      ['objective', [['objectively', 'xolis'], ['objectivity', 'xolislik'], ['subjective', 'sub’ektiv']], 'He speaks *objectively*.']
    ],
    col: [['break the news', 'xabarni yetkazmoq', 'He *broke the news* to us.'], ['hit the headlines', 'sarlavhalarga chiqmoq', 'The story *hit the headlines*.'], ['read the news', 'yangilik o‘qimoq', 'I *read the news* daily.'], ['go to press', 'bosmaga ketmoq', 'The paper *went to press*.']],
    pv: [['look into', 'tekshirmoq', 'Police will *look into* it.'], ['find out', 'bilib olmoq', 'We *found out* the truth.'], ['carry on', 'davom etmoq', 'The show *carried on*.'], ['cover up', 'yashirmoq', 'They tried to *cover up* the scandal.']],
    use: [['news (u.) vs. a piece of news', 'news — sanalmaydigan; bitta yangilik — a piece of news.', ['The *news is* good.', 'A *piece of news* arrived.']],
          ['hear vs. listen to', 'hear — eshitmoq (beixtiyor); listen to — diqqat bilan eshitmoq.', ['I *heard* a noise.', 'I *listen to* the radio.']]],
    syn: [['credible', 'trustworthy', 'unreliable'], ['biased', 'one-sided', 'fair'], ['sensational', 'shocking', 'ordinary'], ['mislead', 'deceive', 'inform']],
    ex: [['The ___ on the front page shocked everyone. (sarlavha)', 'headline'], ['A good journalist always protects his ___ . (manba)', 'source'], ['The video ___ in just two days. (tez ommalashdi)', 'went viral'], ['Always ___ the facts before you share them. (tasdiqlamoq)', 'verify'], ['A ___ article does not take sides. (xolis)', 'objective'], ['The TV ___ read the main news. (boshlovchi)', 'anchor']]
  }
