  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Dress That Wasn’t Perfect', s: 'To‘yga ko‘ylak tanlayotgan Aziza va modaning qarama-qarshiliklari',
    p: [
      ['Aziza was invited to a wedding and wanted a beautiful [outfit]. She walked from shop to shop, looking at every [garment]. Although she liked [elegant] clothes, her sister preferred [casual] ones. “I love [stylish] things,” Aziza said, “whereas you want [baggy] jeans!” In one shop she found a [vintage] dress with a [denim] belt. It had a pretty [pattern], but the [sleeves|sleeve] were too long and the [collar] was strange.',
       'Azizani to‘yga taklif qilishdi va u chiroyli kiyim to‘plamini xohladi. U do‘konma-do‘kon yurib, har bir kiyimga qaradi. Nafis kiyimlarni yoqtirsa-da, opasi kundalik kiyimni afzal ko‘rardi. «Men zamonaviy narsalarni yaxshi ko‘raman, — dedi Aziza, — sen esa keng jinsi xohlaysan!» Bir do‘konda u jinsi kamarli vintaj ko‘ylakni topdi. Unda chiroyli naqsh bor edi, lekin yenglar juda uzun, yoqasi esa g‘alati edi.'],
      ['The seller said she could [take in|take in] the dress. “The [fabric] is high quality, and the [stitches|stitch] are neat,” she explained. “But it is [tailor-made], so it’s not [off the peg|off the peg].” The dress was beautiful, but it would [cost a fortune|cost a fortune]. Aziza checked the [label]: silk and [velvet]. She wanted the [linen] version too, a [formal] cut, with soft [stripes|stripe]. “Despite the price, it is [flattering],” she thought, “but the [hem] needs work.”',
       'Sotuvchi ko‘ylakni toraytirib berishi mumkinligini aytdi. «Mato yuqori sifatli va choklar tartibli, — tushuntirdi u. — Lekin u buyurtma bilan tikilgan, tayyor kiyim emas.» Ko‘ylak chiroyli edi, lekin juda qimmatga tushardi. Aziza yorliqni tekshirdi: ipak va baxmal. U zig‘ir matodan rasmiy kesimdagi yo‘l-yo‘l versiyasini ham xohladi. «Narxiga qaramay, u yarashadi, — deb o‘yladi u, — lekin etagiga ishlov kerak.»'],
      ['In the end she decided to [sew|sew] some parts herself. She bought a cheaper dress, a [bracelet] and a [necklace] as [accessories|accessory], and used a few [stitches|stitch] to fix the [hem] and decided to [embroider] a flower. “This will [go with|go with] my coat,” she said, and showed her sister how to [tuck in|tuck in] the belt. Her sister [dressed down|dress down] and wore jeans, but still looked great. “Neither of us wants to [follow the crowd|follow the crowd],” they agreed.',
       'Oxir-oqibat u ba’zi qismlarni o‘zi tikishga qaror qildi. U arzonroq ko‘ylak, aksessuar sifatida bilaguzuk va bo‘yinbog‘ sotib oldi va etakni tuzatish uchun bir necha chok qo‘ydi va gul kashta tikishga qaror qildi. «Bu paltomga mos keladi», dedi u va opasiga kamarni qanday ichiga tiqishni ko‘rsatdi. Opasi oddiyroq kiyinib, jinsi kiydi, lekin baribir ajoyib ko‘rindi. «Ikkalamiz ham ko‘pchilikka ergashishni xohlamaymiz», deb kelishdi.'],
      ['At the wedding Aziza felt [dressed to kill|dressed to kill]. A friend asked, “Is that dress [in fashion|in fashion]?” Aziza laughed. “Maybe it is [outdated], maybe not. A [hand-me-down] from my grandmother taught me that real style never dies.” The old shoes might [wear out|wear out], she said, but a beautiful idea doesn’t. At the end of the night she wanted to [stand out|stand out] only one thing: her smile.',
       'To‘yda Aziza o‘zini ko‘z qamashtirgudek kiyingandek his qildi. Do‘sti so‘radi: «Bu ko‘ylak modadami?» Aziza kuldi. «Balki eskirgandir, balki yo‘q. Buvimdan qolgan kiyim menga haqiqiy uslub hech qachon o‘lmasligini o‘rgatdi.» Eski poyabzal eskirishi mumkin, dedi u, lekin chiroyli g‘oya eskirmaydi. Kechaning oxirida u faqat bitta narsani ko‘rsatmoqchi edi: tabassumini.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What did Aziza want for the wedding?', ['A beautiful outfit', 'A new bag', 'A taxi'], 0],
      ['What was wrong with the vintage dress?', ['The sleeves were too long.', 'It was torn.', 'It was green.'], 0],
      ['What did Aziza do at last?', ['She bought a cheaper dress and fixed it.', 'She bought nothing.', 'She borrowed a dress.'], 0],
      ['What did her sister wear?', ['Jeans', 'A suit', 'A skirt'], 0],
      ['What did Aziza say about style?', ['Real style never dies.', 'It is expensive.', 'It is boring.'], 0]
    ]
  }],
