  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Teacher Who Loved Word Families', s: 'Lingvist Kamilaning so‘zlarga bo‘lgan muhabbati talabalarni qanday o‘zgartirdi',
    p: [
      ['Kamila was a teacher who believed that [happiness] begins with words. Her students were often [unhappy] with grammar, because they felt it was [impossible] to remember everything. “I [disagree],” Kamila said. “You [underestimate] yourselves. Don’t [misunderstand] me — the secret is not memorising, but understanding how words are made.” Her [co-worker] laughed at her passion, but she was patient and [responsible].',
       'Kamila baxt so‘zlardan boshlanadi, deb ishonadigan o‘qituvchi edi. Uning o‘quvchilari ko‘pincha grammatikadan norozi edi, chunki hammasini eslab qolish imkonsiz tuyulardi. «Men rozi emasman, — dedi Kamila. — Siz o‘zingizni kam baholayapsiz. Meni noto‘g‘ri tushunmang — sir yodlashda emas, so‘zlar qanday yasalishini tushunishda.» Hamkasbi uning ishtiyoqiga kuldi, lekin u sabrli va mas’uliyatli edi.'],
      ['At the board she wrote the word “create” and added [kindness] and [enjoyment] to the lesson. “Each word has a family,” she said. “[Development] of vocabulary is the result of a good [relationship] with language.” She told them that [leadership] means courage, [freedom] means choice, [boredom] is the enemy, and [wisdom] comes from reading. “Try not to [overcook] your sentences — keep them simple, and [rewrite] them when needed.”',
       'Doskada u «create» so‘zini yozdi va darsga mehribonlik va zavq qo‘shdi. «Har bir so‘zning oilasi bor, — dedi u. — Lug‘at rivoji tilga yaxshi munosabatning natijasi.» U yetakchilik — jasorat, erkinlik — tanlov, zerikish — dushman, donolik esa o‘qishdan keladi, dedi. «Gaplaringizni ortiqcha pishirib yubormang — ularni oddiy qiling va kerak bo‘lsa qayta yozing.»'],
      ['One student, Jasur, was [antisocial] and rarely spoke. After a month he showed a surprising [ability] to invent new words. “There is a [possibility] I will become a writer,” he said. His [optimism] was [powerful]. “It is not [hopeless] to learn English,” he added. Kamila’s class studied [tourism] and [harmony] too, imagining a [kingdom] where every citizen speaks two languages. For Jasur, it was a [useful] and [enjoyable] game.',
       'Bitta o‘quvchi, Jasur, kamsuqum edi va kamdan-kam gapirardi. Bir oydan keyin u yangi so‘zlar o‘ylab topishda kutilmagan qobiliyat ko‘rsatdi. «Men yozuvchi bo‘lishim ehtimoli bor», dedi u. Uning optimizmi kuchli edi. «Ingliz tilini o‘rganish umidsiz emas», deb qo‘shdi u. Kamilaning sinfi turizm va uyg‘unlikni ham o‘rgandi, har bir fuqaro ikki tilda gapiradigan qirollikni tasavvur qildi. Jasur uchun bu foydali va yoqimli o‘yin edi.'],
      ['At the end of the year they held a presentation. A [successful] writer visited them and spoke about [reality]. He said that [criticism] hurts, but [generosity] and respect help more. “I learned my craft [effortlessly] only after I understood word families,” he said. A [valuable] gift was given to each student: a notebook for the [homeless] children’s centre. Kamila smiled. “You see, words build [harmony],” she said. And Jasur, once [unhappy], could not stop smiling.',
       'Yil oxirida ular taqdimot o‘tkazdi. Muvaffaqiyatli yozuvchi ularni ziyorat qilib, haqiqat haqida gapirdi. U tanqid og‘riq beradi, lekin saxovat va hurmat ko‘proq yordam beradi, dedi. «Men o‘z hunarimni so‘z oilalarini tushungandan keyingina qiynalmasdan o‘rgandim», dedi u. Har bir o‘quvchiga qimmatli sovg‘a berildi: uysiz bolalar markazi uchun daftar. Kamila jilmaydi. «Ko‘ryapsizlarmi, so‘zlar uyg‘unlik yaratadi», dedi u. Va bir paytlar baxtsiz bo‘lgan Jasur jilmayishdan to‘xtay olmasdi.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What did Kamila believe?', ['Happiness begins with words.', 'Grammar is useless.', 'Reading is boring.'], 0],
      ['What was Jasur like at first?', ['Antisocial and quiet', 'Rich', 'Lazy'], 0],
      ['What did the class imagine?', ['A kingdom where everyone speaks two languages', 'A big city', 'A school'], 0],
      ['What did the visiting writer say hurts?', ['Criticism', 'Praise', 'Silence'], 0],
      ['What did the students get as a gift?', ['A notebook for a children’s centre', 'Money', 'Books'], 0]
    ]
  }],
