      ['“Time passes [in the blink of an eye|in the blink of an eye],” Grandma sighed. “Your first day of school, your first [milestone]… and now you are an [adolescent]. [Adolescence] is a [rite of passage|rite of passage].” Sevara said that she [looked back|look back] with a smile, though she hoped to become [independent] soon. “Soon I will reach [adulthood],” she added. She had [grown out of|grow out of] her fears, such as the dark. “That story is [as old as the hills|as old as the hills],” Grandma laughed.',
       '«Vaqt ko‘z ochib yumguncha o‘tadi, — xo‘rsindi buvisi. — Maktabdagi birinchi kuning, birinchi bosqich… endi sen o‘smirsan. O‘smirlik — kamolot marosimi.» Sevara ortga qarab jilmayib eslayotganini aytdi, garchi tez orada mustaqil bo‘lishga umid qilsa ham. «Tez orada balog‘atga yetaman», deb qo‘shdi u. U qorong‘ilik kabi qo‘rquvlaridan o‘sib o‘tgan edi. «Bu hikoya juda eski», kuldi buvisi.'],
      ['They also found photos of important events: a [christening], a [graduation ceremony], an [jubilee] party for her parents, and a [funeral] of her great-grandfather. Grandma had [moved house|move house] twice, [started school|start school] at six, and [got a job|get a job] at twenty. Now she enjoyed her [retirement] as a [pensioner]. “Every [memorable] moment is a gift,” Grandma said. A [coming-of-age] story was starting for Sevara, and she closed the album carefully.',
       'Ular shuningdek muhim voqealar suratlarini ham topishdi: cho‘qintirish, bitiruv marosimi, ota-onasining yubiley ziyofati va katta bobosining dafn marosimi. Buvisi ikki marta ko‘chgan, olti yoshda maktabga borgan va yigirma yoshda ish topgan edi. Endi u pensioner sifatida nafaqaga chiqqanidan zavq olardi. «Har bir esda qoladigan lahza — sovg‘a», dedi buvisi. Sevara uchun voyaga yetish hikoyasi boshlanayotgan edi va u albomni ehtiyotkorlik bilan yopdi.']
