  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Noisy Neighbour', s: 'Ikki qo‘shni va bir mushuk',
    p: [
      ['Aziza lived on a quiet [estate] with a small [hedge] in front of her house. She and the other [residents|resident] were all [on good terms|on good terms], and they used to [call round|call round] for tea. When she went on holiday, a neighbour would [look after|look after] her cat and [keep an eye on|keep an eye on] her windows. The only [nuisance] was Mr Karimov next door. He was [grumpy] and rarely smiled. Still, neighbours should [look out for|look out for] each other.',
       'Aziza tinch uylar majmuasida, uyi oldida kichik tirik devor bilan yashardi. U va boshqa aholi hammasi yaxshi munosabatda edi, choy ichgani bir-birinikiga kirib turardi. U ta’tilga ketganda, qo‘shnisi mushugiga qarab turardi va derazalariga ko‘z-quloq bo‘lardi. Yagona bezovtalik — yonidagi janob Karimov edi. U jizzaki edi va kamdan-kam jilmayardi.'],
      ['One night the [loud music] and the [barking] from his house started again. Aziza decided not to [gossip about|gossip about] him, because [gossip] only makes trouble. Instead, she walked to his [doorstep] and rang the [doorbell]. “Sorry to [bother] you,” she said, “but could you [keep it down|keep it down]? We cannot sleep.” Mr Karimov looked surprised. Behind the [curtain] of the window, a very [nosy] woman from the next street was watching them.',
       'Bir kechasi uning uyidan baland musiqa va akillash yana boshlandi. Aziza uning haqida mish-mish gapirmaslikka qaror qildi. Buning o‘rniga u ostonasiga bordi va qo‘ng‘iroqni bosdi. «Xalaqit bergan bo‘lsam, uzr, — dedi u, — ovozni pasaytira olasizmi? Biz uxlay olmayapmiz.» Janob Karimov hayron bo‘ldi. Deraza pardasi orqasida keyingi ko‘chadan bir o‘z burnini suqadigan ayol ularga qarab turardi.'],
      ['The next morning Mr Karimov [bumped into|bump into] Aziza and said sorry. He had a new puppy that was [disturbing|disturb] everyone. They [made up|make up] and became friends. He asked for a [favour]: to see the [notice board] for dog trainers. After that, they used to [get along|get along] very well, and no one ever wanted to [fall out|fall out] again. Their [landlady], who owned the [lease], smiled at the end of the month.',
       'Ertasi kuni ertalab janob Karimov Azizani tasodifan uchratdi va uzr so‘radi. Uning yangi kuchukchasi hammani bezovta qilayotgan edi. Ular yarashdilar va do‘st bo‘lishdi. U yaxshilik so‘radi: it o‘rgatuvchilar uchun e’lonlar taxtasini ko‘rib bering. Shundan keyin ular juda yaxshi chiqisha boshladi va hech kim yana janjallashishni xohlamadi. Ijara shartnomasiga ega uy egasi oy oxirida jilmaydi.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['Who was a nuisance for Aziza?', ['Mr Karimov', 'Her sister', 'The landlady'], 0],
      ['What did Aziza do about the noise?', ['She rang his doorbell and asked politely.', 'She called the police.', 'She shouted from the window.'], 0],
      ['What was the real cause of the barking?', ['A new puppy', 'A loud TV', 'A visitor'], 0],
      ['How did the neighbours end?', ['They made up and became friends.', 'They moved away.', 'They never spoke again.'], 0],
      ['Who watched them behind the curtain?', ['A nosy woman', 'A policeman', 'A child'], 0]
    ]
  }],
